 "story": {
  "kicker": "Bywater",
  "h2": "B J's Lounge",
  "paragraphs": [
   "BJ's is the white clapboard corner building on Burgundy, down at the Poland Avenue end of the Bywater, with a mural of a man in a crown playing guitar painted across the side wall. The doors are green and layered in flyers. NO DOGS INSIDE is taped to the grille, ICY COLD BEERS is painted on the jamb, and there are usually a couple of bikes locked to the post out front. Inside, a hand-painted sign hangs over the room that reads BJ's, your 9th Ward Living Room, and the wall beneath it is papered floor to ceiling in snapshots of people who drink here.",
   "Music is the whole reason. A chalkboard goes out on the sidewalk with the week written on it in colored chalk, MONDAY RED BEANS and BLUES across the top and the names underneath changing: Washboard Chaz, Jonathan Frelich, whoever is around. Monday is the big one, red beans cooked in pots behind the bar and set out free while the band plays. Out back there is a yard with its own stage and a sign that says BJ's 9th Ward Backyard, which is where the night goes when the room gets full. Pool table, video poker along the wall, and a jukebox for the nights nobody is playing."
  ]
 },
 "facts": [
  "Live music and live performances, with bar games when nobody is playing",
  "Outdoor seating in the backyard, plus takeout and delivery",
